        <mxCell id="rxoH3m6sTBeBhxrcS38y-23" value="The VisibilityGraph that does grow/shrink&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;merges the zones and then they are anonymous boundaries with somewhat different geometry than original zones &#39;added together&#39;. When we alert, we need vehicles to know the geometry being alerted against, not the original zone. And the old ids are thrown away so we can&#39;t back reference to the original zone geometries&amp;nbsp; even if we could safely do so.&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;So we can&#39;t tie them&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;back to boundaries and do inside/outside checks using CBoundary, unless we recreate CBoundaries, but then we lose min Altitude and MaxAltitude as well as original Zone IDS!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3782.5" y="839.69" width="317.5" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
